module gunbc.native_frontier_debt

import std.types { List }
import v2.compiler.native_test_vocabulary { NativeTestStage }
import gunbc.witness_v2_native_route {
  NativeRouteTestIdentity, NativeRouteExclusionCause, NativeRouteDivergenceCause
}
import gunbc.native_route_progress_guard { NativeProgressDispositionRow, NativeCauseTransitionRow }

// THE NATIVE V2 FRONTIER ROSTER, ITS VOCABULARY. The standing itself is gunbc.native_frontier_roster
// native_frontier_roster. The roster is the debt the emitted-native compiler owes over the v2.test.*
// universe, one row per identity it does not yet agree on, and nothing else.
//
// WHAT KIND OF LITERAL THIS IS (DESIGN section 5). A monotone debt contract over a closed,
// independently discovered subject universe. The universe is DISCOVERED, never authored: it is the
// set of identities `gunbc.witness_v2_native_route` `native_route_default_pattern` plans, derived
// from the tree's own `v2.test.*` declarations by the emitted binary on every run. The roster
// persists the universe its minting run discovered, so that each later run's discovered universe
// is joined to it at identity grain. Membership is joined
// at identity grain (`NativeRouteTestIdentity`, the same identity type the route, its admission
// and gunbc#12049's progress guard key on), never by count, and every way a row can leave carries
// a typed disposition: the run's own observation of the identity at a better attainment (the row
// is re-minted without it), or a `NativeProgressDispositionRow` beside it when the subject left
// the universe.
//
// WHY A ROW NEVER NAMES AN AGREEMENT. `NativeFrontierDebt` has no agreed arm, so a roster that
// claims a subject passes is not writable. An identity absent from `rows` is one the roster
// asserts the route agrees on; `gunbc.native_frontier_ratchet` refuses any run in which it does
// not, and that refusal is the "zero additions" half of the contract.
//
// WHO WRITES IT. Nobody by hand. A row is produced only by `native_frontier_proposal_lines`,
// rendered by the emitted binary from its own run, and it lands through a reviewed pull request
// that carries the run receipt (host, tested tree, executable, command). It is never merged
// automatically.
//
// WHICH RUN PROPOSES IT (operator ruling 2026-09-27). The native route's REQUIRED lane: its run on
// the merge_group revision executes `//gunbc/instruments:v2-native-frontier`, the emitted binary
// prints the `[native-frontier-roster]` proposal, and the lane publishes it. A mint or re-mint pull
// request carries that one run's proposal verbatim, with `tested_tree` equal to the merge_group
// sha, so the roster's receipt names a revision that was judged on the landing path. No schedule
// and no hand-run produces it: the nightly `native-frontier` workflow that used to was deleted by
// that ruling, and until the lane is live the roster stays unminted
// (gunbc.rung_drop v2_native_frontier_nightly_cadence).
//
// WHEN THE FIRST MINT MAY HAPPEN. A mint makes whatever the run observed the baseline, so a mint
// taken just before a known correctness flip lands records the silently wrong acceptances as
// agreement, and the flip then reads as a loss on every one of them. The first mint is therefore
// taken, from the required lane's run, after the pending flips its minter knows of have landed (2026-09-27: the caret flip,
// gunbc#12392, reason caret_symbol_not_lowered), so their refusals enter as baseline debt. A flip
// landing AFTER a mint is not stranded: gunbc.native_frontier_ratchet admits it per identity as
// `FrontierGrewByOwnedCorrectnessFlip` when its cause is owned and declared in
// v2.workflow.compile_door_cause_ownership known_correctness_flips.
//
// THE STANDING TODAY IS UNMINTED, AND THAT IS A RED, NOT A PASS. No run has yet produced a roster:
// the route's measured wall (gunbc.rung_drop v2_native_route_off_the_merge_path, re-derived by the
// run rather than restated here) does not fit a session, and a roster typed out before a run can
// produce one would be a number copied from nothing. `gunbc.native_frontier_ratchet` answers
// `FrontierUnminted` over this standing: the run is complete and its proposal is printed for
// minting, and the instrument still exits non-zero, because an empty roster read as "no debt"
// would be the vacuous pass section 5 forbids.

type NativeFrontierDebt
  = DebtRefused { stage: NativeTestStage, cause: NativeRouteExclusionCause }
  | DebtDiverged { cause: NativeRouteDivergenceCause }

type NativeFrontierDebtRow {
  identity: NativeRouteTestIdentity
  debt: NativeFrontierDebt
}

// THE RUN A ROSTER WAS MINTED FROM, AS THE BINARY SAW ITSELF. The host that ran it and the command
// are in the minting pull request's body. The binary cannot observe either, and inventing them
// here would be a fabricated field.
type NativeFrontierMintReceipt {
  tested_tree: String
  preparation_seed_identity: String
  emitted_closure_identity: String
  executable_identity: String
}

// THE MINTED UNIVERSE IS PERSISTED BESIDE THE DEBT, because "absent from `rows`" can only mean
// "agreed" relative to a universe the roster itself names. Without it, deleting a subject that
// agreed left no trace. The next run's universe was simply smaller, every debt row still matched,
// and the removal passed with no disposition (review, 2026-09-25). With it, every identity in the
// minted universe is a baseline: a debt row where one exists, BaselineAgreed otherwise
// (gunbc.native_route_progress_guard's own vocabulary; NativeFrontierDebt gains no agreed arm).
// So a vanished or renamed identity owes a typed disposition whether it agreed or refused.
type NativeFrontierRosterStanding
  = RosterUnminted
  | RosterMinted {
      receipt: NativeFrontierMintReceipt
      universe: List<NativeRouteTestIdentity>
      rows: List<NativeFrontierDebtRow>
      dispositions: List<NativeProgressDispositionRow>
      cause_transitions: List<NativeCauseTransitionRow>
    }

